{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "traffic-reporter",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-15",
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "triggers": {
    // V1.6.1: every 10 minutes, UTC (Cloudflare Cron Triggers are always
    // UTC; UTC minutes == Asia/Taipei minutes since Taipei is a fixed
    // UTC+8 offset). PBS runs every tick (24/7). TDX (國道+省道 only —
    // see src/tdx/sources.js's PRODUCTION_TDX_SOURCE_IDS) is further
    // gated INSIDE the scheduled handler to only every 2nd tick
    // (minute 00/20/40) and only 08:00–21:59:59 Asia/Taipei — see
    // src/traffic/tdxSchedule.js. Deliberately still just ONE Cron
    // trigger, not two competing schedules — "不要建立兩套互相複雜的
    // Cron".
    "crons": ["*/10 * * * *"]
  },
  // TRAFFIC_KV was originally bound only via the Cloudflare dashboard,
  // which `wrangler deploy` silently dropped on the next deploy because
  // this file is treated as the full declarative binding set (exactly
  // the caveat this comment used to warn about). Declared explicitly now
  // with the real namespace ID from the dashboard so it survives every
  // deploy. TDX_CLIENT_ID/TDX_CLIENT_SECRET/LINE_CHANNEL_ACCESS_TOKEN/
  // LINE_CHANNEL_SECRET remain Cloudflare Secrets configured outside this
  // repo — see src/traffic/dedupe.js — and are unaffected by this change.
  //
  // V1.6.3: ADMIN_PASSWORD (HTTP Basic Auth for GET /health,
  // /debug/status, /debug/tdx, /debug/pbs, /debug/pbs-vpc-probe — see
  // src/security/adminAuth.js) is ALSO a Cloudflare Secret configured
  // outside this repo (`wrangler secret put`), never declared here —
  // this file never carries real credential values, only bindings/IDs
  // that are not secret on their own. The admin username is a fixed
  // constant ("admin") in code, not a Secret — no first-run setup page,
  // no Cookie session, no password ever stored in KV.
  "kv_namespaces": [
    {
      "binding": "TRAFFIC_KV",
      "id": "a763ccea75b0481aa4da99fa43f8341a"
    }
  ],
  // V1.8.4: CCTV_IMAGES — an R2 bucket binding for the published-collage-
  // image layer (src/cctv/publishedImage.js). Deliberately R2, not
  // TRAFFIC_KV: R2 gives strongly consistent read-after-write on
  // PUT/GET/DELETE, which the intended flow (compose -> store ->
  // immediately push to LINE -> LINE's servers GET the URL, likely from
  // a different Cloudflare location) actually needs — Workers KV is only
  // eventually consistent (Cloudflare's own docs: a write can take 60s+
  // to become visible elsewhere, and negative lookups get cached too),
  // which is unacceptable for incident-time delivery. No Secret/API
  // token is required for an R2 Worker binding.
  //
  // CONFIRMED created in Production (post-V1.8.4): bucket enabled, R2
  // lifecycle rule set to auto-delete objects after 1 day — a backstop
  // ONLY, never what determines a published-image URL's validity; that's
  // still enforced entirely in code from each object's own
  // customMetadata.expiresAt on every read (see publishedImage.js).
  "r2_buckets": [
    {
      "binding": "CCTV_IMAGES",
      "bucket_name": "traffic-reporter-cctv-images"
    }
  ],
  // V1.8.5: PUBLIC_BASE_URL — this Worker's own public HTTPS origin, NOT
  // a secret (LINE's servers already need to fetch from it with zero
  // credential — see cctv/publishedImage.js). Needed because the dynamic
  // per-accident CCTV image URL (cctv/dynamicCollage.js) is built from
  // the Cron scheduled handler, which has no incoming Request to derive
  // an origin from the way the Admin HTTP endpoints do (see
  // hsinchuCctvProbe.js's handleHsinchuCctvPublishTest). Code falls back
  // to this exact value if the var is ever absent/misconfigured, so a
  // missing var degrades safely rather than producing a broken URL.
  "vars": {
    "PUBLIC_BASE_URL": "https://traffic-reporter.mr-happytan.workers.dev",
    // TDX QUOTA PROTECTION (2026-08-23). "PBS_ONLY" stops every TDX API
    // call from the Cron path (RoadEvent freeway/highway, the OAuth token,
    // and CCTV enrichment) while 警廣 PBS keeps running unchanged.
    // TDX code is NOT removed — this is a runtime gate.
    // RESTORE: set this to "ALL" (or delete the var) and push to main.
    // Full procedure: src/traffic/sourceMode.js module comment.
    // It lives here rather than in the dashboard because Workers Builds
    // treats this file as authoritative and would overwrite a
    // dashboard-only var on the next build.
    "TRAFFIC_SOURCE_MODE": "PBS_ONLY",
    // LINE PUSH POLICY (2026-08-23). The LINE OA's monthly proactive-Push
    // allowance is limited, so proactive broadcast is temporarily narrowed
    // to accidents only: closure/control/construction/'other' anomalies and
    // 機動路肩 announcements all stop pushing. Detection of every one of
    // them is UNCHANGED — they still appear in /debug/status and the
    // Pipeline Trace; only the proactive product is withheld.
    // Set to "ALL_ELIGIBLE" to restore the previous behaviour. A typo
    // resolves to the restrictive default on purpose (the expensive
    // mistake here is pushing too much). Rule: src/traffic/broadcastPolicy.js.
    "LINE_PUSH_POLICY": "MAJOR_ACCIDENT_ONLY",
    // V2.0.2 (Config Drift Hotfix) — PBS_AI_DECISION_ENABLED lived ONLY as
    // a Dashboard Variable from V1.9.9 Phase 3D through V2.0.1. Same root
    // cause as TRAFFIC_SOURCE_MODE's own comment above: Workers Builds
    // treats THIS FILE as authoritative on every deploy, so a
    // Dashboard-only var is silently dropped the next time main is
    // pushed — GPT Work's manual "true" setting was removed by a later
    // deployment, and AI decisions fell back to the code-level default
    // (false) without anyone changing PBS_AI_DECISION_ENABLED on
    // purpose. wrangler.jsonc / GitHub main is now the ONE canonical
    // source of truth for this var — the Dashboard is no longer used to
    // set it long-term. MUST be the STRING "true" (Cloudflare injects
    // Workers Variables as strings, never real booleans — see
    // src/pbs/aiConfig.js#resolvePbsAiDecisionEnabled(), which accepts
    // this exact string form since V1.9.9 Phase 3D). To disable AI
    // decisions, change this value here and push — never rely on a
    // Dashboard-only override again.
    "PBS_AI_DECISION_ENABLED": "true",
    // V2.4.0 (TDX_FREEWAY_PROVINCIAL_TO_UNIFIED_AI_PIPELINE) — three
    // granular TDX switches, ADDITIONAL to (never a replacement for)
    // TRAFFIC_SOURCE_MODE above — order section 四's own explicit
    // instruction was NOT to flip TRAFFIC_SOURCE_MODE back to "ALL".
    // Full reasoning: src/traffic/sourceMode.js's own V2.4.0 comment
    // block. All three default OFF ("false") on purpose — this round
    // BUILDS the TDX-RoadEvent-to-Queue-to-AI mechanism and its own test
    // suite proves it works, but does not itself begin spending real TDX
    // quota or enqueueing anything; a human operator flips these when
    // ready to begin Phase A/B (see this round's own final report/
    // 07_KNOWN_ISSUES.md for the phase model). MUST be the STRING "true"
    // to turn on (same Cloudflare-injects-strings discipline as every
    // other var in this block) — anything else, including a typo, stays
    // off.
    //
    // TDX_ROADEVENT_FETCH_ENABLED — Phase A gate: may the Cron path fetch
    // TDX freeway/highway RoadEvent data at all this tick.
    //
    // V2_4_0_PHASE_A_TDX_FETCH_ONLY_ENABLE (2026-09-01): flipped on.
    // FETCH ONLY — TDX_ROADEVENT_QUEUE_INGRESS_ENABLED stays "false" right
    // below, so a fetched TDX event is still never enqueued onto
    // PBS_AI_QUEUE, never reaches AI, and can never produce a real LINE
    // push (see debugPush.js's own suppressLineNotify hardcoding, which
    // this round did not touch). This switch alone only lets
    // scheduled.js's own fetch/normalize/dedupe/service-area-filter logic
    // run against real TDX Freeway/Highway RoadEvent data for observation.
    "TDX_ROADEVENT_FETCH_ENABLED": "true",
    // TDX_ROADEVENT_QUEUE_INGRESS_ENABLED — Phase B gate: may a fetched
    // new/updated TDX event be enqueued onto PBS_AI_QUEUE for AI
    // judgment. Even when true, TDX-origin candidates never reach a real
    // LINE push in this version of the code (see debugPush.js's own
    // V2.4.0 comment on why Phase C requires a future CODE change, not a
    // config flip) — this switch alone can only ever reach Phase B.
    //
    // V2_4_0_PHASE_B_QUEUE_OBSERVE_ENABLE (2026-09-01): flipped on.
    // AI OBSERVE ONLY — a genuinely new/updated TDX Freeway/Highway
    // RoadEvent now reaches PBS_AI_QUEUE and the shared AI engine, with
    // Recent Incident Memory context. TDX LINE/CCTV/R2 stay structurally
    // blocked (runAiApprovedPbsBroadcast's suppressLineNotify check now
    // runs BEFORE CCTV preparation, not just before the LINE push — see
    // that function's own V2_4_0_PHASE_B_QUEUE_OBSERVE_ENABLE comment).
    "TDX_ROADEVENT_QUEUE_INGRESS_ENABLED": "true",
    // TDX_ROADEVENT_PRODUCTION_NOTIFY_ENABLED — Phase C gate (new,
    // V2_4_0_PHASE_C_PRODUCTION_NOTIFY_IMPLEMENTATION, 2026-09-01).
    // Default "false" — a TDX-origin AI notify:true event still does 0
    // LINE / 0 CCTV prepare / 0 R2 publish, exactly like Phase B, just now
    // via a canonical config switch instead of a hardcoded source check
    // (see src/pbs/debugPush.js's own comment on suppressLineNotify).
    // MUST be the string "true" to lift the suppression — this round
    // builds and tests the mechanism but does NOT flip it; enabling real
    // TDX LINE delivery requires a separate, explicit future human
    // authorization order.
    "TDX_ROADEVENT_PRODUCTION_NOTIFY_ENABLED": "false",
    // TDX_CCTV_METADATA_REFRESH_ENABLED — independent of the switches
    // above: may /admin/cctv-hsinchu-probe actually call TDX to refresh
    // cctv:freeway-metadata:v1. CCTV metadata refresh stays manual/
    // on-demand either way (order section 三) — this only decides whether
    // that manual trigger itself is allowed to make its one TDX call.
    "TDX_CCTV_METADATA_REFRESH_ENABLED": "false"
  },
  "vpc_services": [
    {
      "binding": "PBS_RELAY_WINDOWS",
      "service_id": "01a008ab-4cc4-7c22-a747-4e27cdcc83c8"
    }
  ],
  // V1.9.9 Phase 3B — Workers AI binding for Windows PBS driver-impact
  // decisions (src/pbs/aiDecisionEngine.js, model '@cf/zai-org/glm-4.7-flash').
  // Declaring this binding here does NOT by itself turn AI decisions on —
  // that gate is the "vars" block's own PBS_AI_DECISION_ENABLED above
  // (see its own V2.0.2 comment for why it now lives here, canonically,
  // instead of only in the Dashboard).
  "ai": {
    "binding": "AI"
  },
  // V2.3.0 (PBS AI Queue Reliability) — the ONE Cloudflare Queue this
  // project uses (order's own "只建立一條 Queue" rule — no separate PBS/
  // AI/LINE/Observatory queues). Producer: src/pbs/debugPush.js's
  // handlePbsDebugPush (POST /internal/pbs-debug-push). Consumer: the
  // SAME traffic-reporter Worker's own `queue()` export (src/index.js) —
  // no separate Worker/project, per the order's own "不要為此拆新專案".
  //
  // WHY THIS LIVES HERE, CANONICALLY (same reasoning as TRAFFIC_SOURCE_MODE/
  // PBS_AI_DECISION_ENABLED's own comments above): Workers Builds treats
  // this file as authoritative on every deploy. A Queue producer/consumer
  // binding declared ONLY in the Dashboard would risk the exact same
  // silent-drop failure mode those vars already suffered — this file is
  // the ONE canonical source of truth for this binding, never the
  // Dashboard.
  //
  // REAL QUEUE RESOURCE — NOT independently verifiable as already existing
  // from this sandbox (no live Cloudflare API/Dashboard access; same
  // structural limitation as every other "real Production state" fact
  // this repo's own Engineering Memory already discloses honestly). If
  // the queue named below does not yet exist in the real Cloudflare
  // account, it must be created (e.g. `wrangler queues create
  // pbs-ai-processing-queue`, or via the Dashboard) BEFORE this config can
  // deploy successfully — see this round's own final report's
  // BROWSER_ACTION_REQUIRED field.
  "queues": {
    "producers": [
      {
        "queue": "pbs-ai-processing-queue",
        "binding": "PBS_AI_QUEUE"
      }
    ],
    "consumers": [
      {
        "queue": "pbs-ai-processing-queue",
        // Deliberately 1 — one Worker invocation per event keeps
        // per-message ack/retry reasoning as simple as possible for this
        // project's real traffic pattern (tens of events/day, never
        // bursty) — order's own "不要過度設計" precedent, same reasoning
        // this repo already applies to KV_ONLY_ATOMICITY.
        "max_batch_size": 1,
        // Matches src/pbs/debugPush.js's own exported MAX_QUEUE_RETRIES —
        // that code's own bail-out (author a deterministic
        // PROCESSING_FAILED terminal state) fires at exactly this
        // boundary, so a real DLQ/drop from the platform is never relied
        // upon to explain a final failure.
        "max_retries": 3
      }
    ]
  }
}
